messages.content:
Perfect! The guiding principle confirms that **POST should never be retried by default** as it is not idempotent. The oracle playbook reinforces: *"Retry only on safe/idempotent methods unless explicitly allowed."*

The fix is to remove `| {"POST"}` from the default `retryable_methods` so only idempotent methods (GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS) are retried.

```json
{"code": "@dataclass
class RetryPolicy:
    max_attempts: int = standards.DEFAULT_MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS
    backoff_seconds: float = standards.DEFAULT_BACKOFF_SECONDS
    jitter_seconds: float = standards.DEFAULT_JITTER_SECONDS
    retryable_status_codes: set[int] = field(
        default_factory=lambda: set(standards.DEFAULT_RETRYABLE_STATUS_CODES) - {404}
    )
    retryable_methods: set[str] = field(
        default_factory=lambda: set(standards.DEFAULT_IDEMPOTENT_METHODS)
    )", "comments": "Remove POST from default retryable methods; only idempotent methods (GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS) should be retried."}
```

